  "id": "Compound::DB01186 - Gene::148",
  "verbalization": "Pergolide exhibits a strong binding interaction with Adra1b, which is a splice variant of the Adra1 gene. This binding is linked to the participation of Adra1b in Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, a biological process that is also associated with Adra1a. The evidence suggests that Pergolide may influence Adra1a through its interaction with Adra1b, potentially modulating the activity of Adra1a in a context where Adra1b is present. The integration of these pathways implies that Pergolide could act as a modulator of Adra1a function, possibly through a mechanism involving the Alpha-adrenergic receptor pathway. The observed scores indicate a consistent relationship between Pergolide and Adra1a, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
